{"subject": "maths", "level": "ibdp", "topic_display": "Statistics & Probability", "topic_slug": "statistics--probability", "theme": "maths-grid", "adventure_n": 1, "title": "Random Variables and Expectation", "emoji": "🎲", "welcome_lead": "Quantify uncertainty: compute expectation and variance for random variables.", "meta_desc": "Maths adventure on discrete random variables, E(X), Var(X) and distributions.", "final_note": "E(X) is the long-run average, Var(X) the spread squared!", "concepts": [{"term": "Random variable", "def": "Variable whose value depends on a random event."}, {"term": "Discrete RV", "def": "Takes countable values like 0, 1, 2,."}, {"term": "Continuous RV", "def": "Takes any value in an interval, e.g. heights."}, {"term": "Expectation", "def": "E(X) = Σ x P(X = x) for discrete X."}, {"term": "Variance", "def": "Var(X) = E(X^2) - (E(X))^2."}, {"term": "Standard deviation", "def": "σ = √Var(X), measures average spread."}], "walkthroughs": [{"tag": "exp", "h2": "Compute Expectation", "body_html": "<p>X has P(0) = 0.2, P(1) = 0.5, P(2) = 0.3.</p><p>E(X) = 0(0.2) + 1(0.5) + 2(0.3) = 0.5 + 0.6 = 1.1.</p>"}, {"tag": "var", "h2": "Compute Variance", "body_html": "<p>From above, E(X^2) = 0 + 0.5 + 4(0.3) = 1.7.</p><p>Var(X) = 1.7 - 1.1^2 = 1.7 - 1.21 = 0.49.</p>"}, {"tag": "ev2", "h2": "Linear Property", "body_html": "<p>If E(X) = 5, find E(3X + 2).</p><p>E(3X+2) = 3E(X) + 2 = 15 + 2 = 17.</p>"}], "mcqs": [{"q": "Formula for E(X) discrete?", "options": [["Σ x P(X=x)", 1], ["Σ P(X=x)", 0], ["x × P(X=x) max", 0], ["∫ x f(x) dx", 0]]}, {"q": "Var(X) equals?", "options": [["E(X^2) - (E(X))^2", 1], ["E(X)^2 - E(X^2)", 0], ["E(X) × 2", 0], ["Σ P(x)", 0]]}], "numericals": [{"q": "Fair die expectation E(X)?", "options": [3, 3.5, 4, 6], "answer": 3.5}], "free_texts": [{"q": "Symbol for standard deviation?", "answer": "sigma"}]}